    "Shared identity-owned transactional adoption store used by the platform-authorized HTTP service and explicit offline installation adapter",
    "Offline adapter is not a Spring component or RPC provider and rejects request, authorization and Spring Security contexts",
    "Technical installation actor recorded without impersonating a human administrator or relying on login to an unadopted personal workspace",
    "Installer tenants-review and tenants-adopt commands bind tenant cohort, actual storage namespace, deployment operation and artifact; current resource definitions are reread at execution without resource-version checks",
    "Stable cursor inventory of all active pending tenants, with explicit bounds and rejection of active tenants lacking setup markers",
    "Per-tenant commits and shared durable installation journal support partial failures and response loss; completed tenants are not reissued rights",
    "Read-back aggregation is compared with durable installation completion even on successful repeated executions",
    "No runtime initializers, HTTP stack, login endpoints, workflow engine or event workers are started by the explicit offline context"
